cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SEER in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: "SEER: Self-Evolving Event Reasoning and Retrieval for Time Series Forecasting"
abstract: >-
  SEER is a closed-loop framework that dynamically optimizes event conditioning for time series
  forecasting. It translates prediction errors into two decoupled feedback mechanisms: a reflective
  retrieval memory that refines subsequent search queries and filters spurious noise, and a
  persistent causal knowledge base that distills transferable domain dynamics. SEER enforces strict
  chronological boundaries across event retrieval and reflection, preventing look-ahead bias and
  data leakage, and consistently outperforms time series foundation models and language model
  baselines across six volatile benchmarks.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/BennyTMT/SEER"
date-released: 2026-10-04
keywords:
